{
  "Document": [
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 1,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "The Build Process"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Turning your code into a distributable application involves several steps of compilation and bundling."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 2,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "How Tauri Builds Your App"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "When you run "
        },
        {
          "InlineCode": "cargo tauri build"
        },
        {
          "Text": ", the following happens:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "OrderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Bold": [
            {
              "Text": "Frontend Compilation"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "Text": ": Tauri runs your frontend build script (e.g., "
        },
        {
          "InlineCode": "trunk build --release"
        },
        {
          "Text": "). This compiles your Leptos Rust code into an optimized WASM binary and generates the HTML/CSS/JS."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "OrderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Bold": [
            {
              "Text": "Backend Compilation"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "Text": ": Cargo compiles the native Rust core with the "
        },
        {
          "InlineCode": "--release"
        },
        {
          "Text": " flag, applying heavy optimizations for speed and size."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "OrderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Bold": [
            {
              "Text": "Asset Bundling"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "Text": ": The WASM and assets are embedded directly into the final native binary."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "OrderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Bold": [
            {
              "Text": "Installer Generation"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "Text": ": Tauri uses system tools (like WiX on Windows or hdiutil on macOS) to wrap the binary in a standard installer ("
        },
        {
          "InlineCode": ".msi"
        },
        {
          "Text": ", "
        },
        {
          "InlineCode": ".dmg"
        },
        {
          "Text": ", "
        },
        {
          "InlineCode": ".deb"
        },
        {
          "Text": ")."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 2,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "Build Times"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "The first build is usually slow because it compiles all dependencies. Subsequent builds are much faster due to Cargo's caching. Use a fast SSD and ensure you have enough RAM to speed up the process."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}